Fixture for the C test suite: tests/xdg-config is exported as XDG_CONFIG_HOME, so
the icon theme is the one this directory names and not whatever the developer runs.

Both files say the same thing because the two toolkits read different ones: a GTK 4
binary reads gtk-4.0/settings.ini and ignores gtk-3.0/settings.ini, so pinning only
the 3.0 file left the tests on the developer's theme -- which is how
`utilities-terminal` came to be missing from a machine that has it.
